ng this all across this  continent at the dinner hour wherever it  was in the eastern time zone of the  central time zone of the Western time so  families would gather in South Dakota we  call it supper around the television  said to watch the news together to get  the first full account of what happened  that day not just in our country but  around the world I was a part of that  audience I was in an impressionable  teenager with a great interest in  American politics and what was going on  in the world and I had my nose press up  against the glass metaphorically of the  screen that delivered to our working  class living room images that had  happened that day in distant places it  was in many ways a transforming  experience because it expanded the  universe occupied not only by those of  us who lived in rural America but  millions of others across the television  landscape we were witnessed in our own  homes to the events that defined our  times wars political conventions and  elections national tragedies great  social causes the civil rights movement  led by dr. Martin Luther King never  would have happened was the same speed  it did without the place of network  television news to bind together this  country the great moral cause finally  recognizing the desperate need to do  something about racial inequality still  for all their illumination these two  planets the CBS Evening News on the NBC  Nightly News with shut and David also  had deep shadow  where other forms of life were not  nurtured racial issues were covered  extensively but gender issues were not  indeed very few women had any role in  reporting or in producing the network  news at the time the race for space was  a marquee event for those early network  broadcasts but the breathtaking advances  that were taking place simultaneously in  the health sciences were little noticed  in foreign news there was a heavy  reliance on Europe and the Middle East  but Asia apart from Vietnam it was a  little about